# Line-ending normalization.
#
# .editorconfig sets `end_of_line = crlf`, and the CI `dotnet format --verify-no-changes`
# gate enforces it. Without an explicit attribute, git stores C# sources as LF and the
# Linux CI runner checks them out as LF, failing the ENDOFLINE rule (Windows working
# trees pass only because core.autocrlf converts to CRLF locally).
#
# Forcing `eol=crlf` guarantees CRLF in the working tree on every platform, including CI.
*.cs      text eol=crlf

# Files that must remain LF for cross-platform / Linux tooling.
*.sh      text eol=lf
